    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know they say things change but it doesnt feel like that. my whole identity was tied to that space. now that it's all wiped, there's nothing left to rebuild. it feels more like a permanent death than just a bad phase. like the person who mattered is actually dead and this is just some leftover shell.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of feeling like a permanent loss is immense, and it's understandable that you feel there's nothing left to anchor yourself to. When your entire sense of self is tied to something that's gone, it can feel like the end of everything. Even when the past self is gone, the capacity to create a new, perhaps different, self is still within you. Please consider talking to someone who can help you explore what might be possible in this new, uncertain space.",
      "source": "target",
